# What is not part of a script.
#
# The engine reads this when pushing a script to a repository: what it excludes
# is left untouched there. The local tooling (scripts/lib/ignore.js) reads the
# same file when it collects a script's assets, so an upload and a push agree
# on what belongs to the script.
#
# Everything below is repository furniture or tooling, plus the notes that live
# beside virtual-world's code and are not assets of it.

/aiwebengine.config.json
/AGENTS.md
/apis
/CLAUDE.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/jsconfig.json
/LICENSE
/Makefile
/node_modules
/package-lock.json
/package.json
/README.md
/schemas
/scripts
/SECURITY.md
/tsconfig.json
/types

# virtual-world's working notes sit next to its code; they are not assets.
/virtual-world/*.md

.DS_Store
